      <div type="clause" n="2.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 2.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.16"/> æfre ænig mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.17"/> heonon forð Godes cyricgrið swa abrece, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he binnon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.18"/> ciricwagum mannslaga weorðe, þonne sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.19"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> botleas, ⁊ ehte his ælc þæra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.20"/> þe Godes freond sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.21"/>, butan þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> geweorðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he þanon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.22"/> ætberste ⁊ swa deope friðsocne gesece, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se cyningc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.23"/> him þurh ðæt feores geunne, wiþ fulre bote ge wið God ge wið menn.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.24"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif æfre anig man heonon forð Godes cyricgrið swa abrece, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he binnan cyricwagum manslaga wæorðe, þonne is þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> botleas, ⁊ ehte his ælc þara þe Godes freond sy, butan þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> geweorðe, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he þano[n]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.4"/> ætberste ⁊ swa deope friðsocne gesece, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> se cyningc hym þurh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feores geunne, wið fulre bote ge wið Godd ge wyð menn.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="280" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis amodo pacem ęcclesię Dei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.2"/> uiolabit, ut inter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.8"/> parietes eius homicidium faciat, hoc inemendabile<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.9"/> sit, et persequatur eum omnis qui Deum diligit, nisi contingat, ut per aliquod pacis confugium rex ei uitam concedat, plenis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.10"/> emendationibus erga Deum et homines.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi dehinc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.8-2"/> aliquis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.9-2"/> pacem ęcclesiarum Dei ita uiolauerit, ut infra parietes homicidium faciat, hoc sit inemendabile, persequaturque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.10-2"/> talem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.11"/> omnis qui uoluerit Dei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.12"/> esse amicus, nisi hoc fiat, ut effugiat et talem locum aut hominem requirat, pro qua<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.13"/> requisitione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.14"/> ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.15"/> rex uitam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.16-2"/> condonet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.17-2"/>, attamen ad plenam emendationem.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.oe.18-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si posthac quisquam Dei ecclesie . . . ., homicida fiat, inemendabile habeatur; et persequatur eum omnis qui Dei sit amicus, nisi hoc fortasse contingat, quod evadens tam dignum locum adeat, quod ea causa rex ei uitam concedat pro plena satisfactione tam erga Deum quam erga homines.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="2.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf æfre ænig mann heonon forð Godes cyricgrið swa abrece þæt he binnon ciricwagum mannslaga weorþe, þonne sig<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-3.robnote.fn.1"/> þæt botleas, ⁊ ehte his ælc þæra þe Godes freond sig, butan þæt geweorðe þæt he þanon ætberste ⁊ swa deope friðsocne gesece, þæt se cyningc him þurh ðæt feores geunne wiþ fulre bote ge wið God ge wið menn.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="232" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf æfre ænig mann heonon forð Godes cyricgrið swa abrece, þæt he binnon ciricwagum mannslaga weorðe, þonne sig þæt botleas, and ehte his ælc þæra þe Godes freond sig, butan þæt geweorðe þæt he þanon ætberste and swa deope friðsocne gesece þæt se cyningc him þurh ðæt feores geunne, wiþ fulre bote ge wið God ge wið menn.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="281" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn je hinfort jemand den Sonderfrieden einer Kirche Gottes so weit verletzt, dass er innerhalb der Kirchenmauern<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.de.1"/> Todtschläger wird, dann sei dies unabbüssbar, und verfolge ihn jeder derer, der Gottes Freund ist; ausser wenn es geschieht, dass er von dannen entkomme und ein so gewichtiges Friedensasyl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-3.lnote.de.2"/> erreiche, dass um dessen willen der König ihm das Leben schenkt, bei voller Busse sowohl gegenüber der Kirche als den Weltlichen:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if ever henceforth anyone so violates the protection of God's church that he becomes a manslayer within the church walls, then that is beyond compensation, and let everyone who is God's friend pursue him; unless it happens that he escapes from there and reaches so weighty a sanctuary that for its sake the king grants him his life, on full compensation both to God and to men:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_2-3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>And if ever anyone henceforth violates the protection of the church of God by committing homicide within its walls, that crime shall not be atoned for by any payment of compensation, and everyone who is the friend of God shall pursue the miscreant, unless it happen that he escapes from there and reaches so inviolable a sanctuary<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_2-3.robnote.n.2"/> that the king, because of that, grants him his life, upon condition that he makes full amends both towards God and towards men.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="233" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And henceforth, if anyone ever violates the sanctuary of God’s church by committing murder within its walls, that violation shall be deemed beyond compensation, and all those who are friends of God shall hunt him down, unless it so happens that he escapes from there and seeks out protection so powerful that the king therefore spares his life as long as he does full penance toward God and the community.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="281"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_1-1">VIII Atr 1.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VIII Atr. 1, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Grith_13">Grið 13</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_1">Leis Wl 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_1-1">VIII Atr 1.1–5.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 2:3-3:2: VIII Atr 1:1-5:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="93"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_1-1">VIII Atr 1.1</ref> <quote>VIII Atr 1:1 = I Cn 2:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="395"><label>earlier version</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_13">Grið 13</ref> <quote>the death penalty for killing within church walls made generally mandatory by VIII Æthelred and Cnut, Grið must have been drafted before 1014</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VIII Atr 1.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 281, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
